The wonderful colchester arts centre and this contains what I think will be the best story of today's exploration of the ancient city of colchester.
这座很棒的科尔切斯特艺术中心，藏着我觉得会是今天探索古城时最精彩的故事。

2
00:00:12,240 --> 00:00:22,870
Cuz it's from this tower here that humpty dumpty had a great fall during the english civil war.
因为作者说，Humpty Dumpty 就是在英国内战期间从这座塔上摔落的。

3
00:00:22,880 --> 00:00:28,440
And I'm ashamed to say I didn't know that humpty dumpty was in fact a massive cannon.
惭愧地说，我竟不知道 Humpty Dumpty 其实是一门巨炮；这是作者对该故事的说法。

4
00:00:29,440 --> 00:00:36,750
And it was during the siege of colchester in the english civil war I'll put the date on the screen but it would have been in the 1640 s.
那是在英国内战的科尔切斯特围城期间，我会把日期放在屏幕上，应该是十七世纪四十年代。

5
00:00:36,760 --> 00:00:53,430
That the massive cannon called humpty dumpty had a great fall from that tower right down here to balkerne hill on the edge of the ancient city of colchester how brilliant.
那门叫 Humpty Dumpty 的巨炮从塔上落到下面的 Balkerne Hill，就在古城边缘；真精彩。

6
00:00:53,440 --> 00:01:05,510
And as an indicator of what lies ahead casually just here next to the colchester arts centre we have part of the original roman wall dating from the 1 st century ad.
这也预示接下来有什么：就在艺术中心旁，随处可见一段原有罗马城墙，作者说始于公元一世纪。

7
00:01:05,520 --> 00:01:19,270
The 1 st century ad this wall is over 2 000 years old just here by the roadside on balkerne hill.
公元一世纪！这面墙有两千多年，就在 Balkerne Hill 的路边；年代依作者说法。

8
00:01:19,280 --> 00:01:31,400
Colchester britain's first recorded city the city of cymbeline shakespeare's cymbeline king cymbeline his real name was something else.
科尔切斯特，英国首个有记录的城市，辛白林之城，莎士比亚笔下的辛白林国王；他的真名另有所指。

9
00:01:31,400 --> 00:01:38,720
But king cymbeline lived here as did obviously we talked to humpty dumpty the cannon that fell from the tower.
但辛白林国王住在这里；当然还有我们说到的 Humpty Dumpty，就是从塔上落下的炮。

10
00:01:38,720 --> 00:01:47,040
And actually what's lovely is you know this is britain's first recorded city city of great history the roman city look this is the roman wall this is mad.
很妙的是，这是英国首个有记录的城市，历史深厚的罗马城市。看，这就是罗马城墙，太不可思议了。

11
00:01:47,040 --> 00:02:01,040
This is probably older than the london roman wall crazy but it's also a land of of nursery rhymes humpty dumpty and twinkle twinkle little star which we will also see in a bit.
它大概比伦敦的罗马城墙还老，真惊人；但这里也是童谣之地，有 Humpty Dumpty 和《小星星》，稍后会看到。

12
00:02:01,040 --> 00:02:09,790
That was written here in the dutch quarter amazing I I just came down here to do a talk this afternoon at the wonderful colchester arts centre.
那首歌写于这里的荷兰区，太棒了。我今天下午只是过来在很棒的艺术中心做一场讲座。

13
00:02:09,800 --> 00:02:17,240
Such lovely wonderful people big shoutout to paul happy birthday to paul my son's friend james who was going to show me around.
大家真好。特别向 Paul 问好，祝他生日快乐；我儿子的朋友 James 原本打算带我逛逛。

14
00:02:17,240 --> 00:02:23,200
But I didn't really organize it with james james will have to fix that and and do it later but big shoutout to james as well.
但我没和 James 安排好，以后得把这事安排上；也向 James 特别致意。

15
00:02:23,600 --> 00:02:31,390
Just the offer of james showing me around offering his great knowledge of town planning would be great so that'll be another video I imagine.
James 提议带我逛，分享他丰富的城市规划知识，光这件事就很棒；我想那会是另一个视频。

16
00:02:31,400 --> 00:02:38,840
And such lovely people in the colchester arts centre what a venue mick fest in august is going to be something I'm going to come back for as well.
艺术中心的人真好，场地真棒；八月的 Mick Fest 我也想再来参加，活动名依字幕待核。

17
00:02:38,840 --> 00:02:46,240
I love colchester already but this is astonishing and of course I deliberately eulogize about history.
我已经喜欢上科尔切斯特了，真令人惊叹；当然，我特意在这里赞叹历史。

18
00:02:46,240 --> 00:02:55,110
By this dual carriageway which runs around the outside of the town centre it must be the city centre right of colchester.
就在绕着镇中心外侧的双向分隔公路旁；应该叫市中心吧，科尔切斯特的市中心。

19
00:02:55,120 --> 00:03:04,550
And up here we have the hole in the wall pub near a hole in the roman wall this looks like one of the bastion gates there doesn't it.
上面是 Hole in the Wall 酒馆，就在罗马城墙的洞口旁。这看起来像一座堡垒城门，对吧？

20
00:03:04,560 --> 00:03:12,560
So here we have the balkerne gate which is the largest roman gateway in britain it tells us here on the information board.
这里是 Balkerne Gate，信息牌说它是英国最大的罗马城门。

21
00:03:12,560 --> 00:03:20,680
Built here as part of a ceremonial arch in ad 49 to mark the foundation of roman colchester.
它作为仪式性拱门的一部分建于公元49年，以纪念罗马科尔切斯特的建立；作者在读现场介绍。

22
00:03:22,840 --> 00:03:35,510
Of course colchester was burnt to the ground in ad 60 by boudica and her followers and they kind of killed everybody here it was quite a brutal attack on the roman garrison.
当然，作者说公元60年布狄卡和追随者把城烧毁，几乎杀了所有人，对罗马驻军的攻击很残酷。

23
00:03:35,520 --> 00:03:42,800
That is really impressive it'd be reason to come to colchester alone just to see this section of roman wall and the balkerne gate.
真令人震撼。单为了看这段罗马城墙和 Balkerne Gate，就足以成为来科尔切斯特的理由。
